E5 exploratory null baselines inside e5.analyse (explore_native_null, all native systems of the analysis so block N needs no change): which white-box cells, zero system, plain RAG and oracle intervals contain each native estimate, inside and discriminating counts for the label-circular (orphan) and out-of-sample comparisons, the counts a label-free baseline gets under the same rule, chance coverage over permuted labels, item-paired native minus predicted cell differences with the interval widened by the repeat-ingestion variance, and B marked unidentified when the persistence interval straddles 0.5; tested on a synthetic three-system fixture with cited-cluster cells, baselines and a second ingestion

